Nexus Engineering has expertise in AI-powered solutions and collaborates with the client's experts to ensure the solution meets their needs. The proposed solution supports health interoperability standards (HL7, FHIR) and integrates with the national health identifier (INS) and national framework (S-GUR du numérique en santé, Mon Espace Santé, DMP). The solution provides assistance in drafting clinical and administrative content, including discharge summaries, medical reports, medical correspondence, patient letters, and administrative documents.

In conclusion, Nexus Engineering's proposal meets the requirements and constraints of the call for tenders, providing an intelligent assistance tool that supports hospital staff in clinical and administrative activities while ensuring data sovereignty, security, and compliance with regulatory requirements. The solution is based on a robust and scalable architecture, deployed on a secure and environmentally friendly infrastructure, and provides a high level of explainability and transparency.
